To prove that the opposite sides of parallelogram $ABCD$ are equal, the diagonal $AC$ is drawn. Which pair of triangles must be proved congruent?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc}
\tikzset{sa/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}},da/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.4 with {\arrow{Stealth}},mark=at position 0.56 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6,2.2);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.2);
\draw[sa] (A)--(B);
\draw[da] (B)--(C);
\draw[sa] (D)--(C);
\draw[da] (A)--(D);
\draw (A)--(C);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the proof that the diagonals of parallelogram $ABCD$ bisect each other at $E$, what is the reason that $\angle BAE = \angle DCE$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc}
\tikzset{sa/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}},da/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.4 with {\arrow{Stealth}},mark=at position 0.56 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6,2.2);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.2);
\draw[sa] (A)--(B);
\draw[da] (B)--(C);
\draw[sa] (D)--(C);
\draw[da] (A)--(D);
\coordinate (E) at (3,1.1);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (B)--(D);
\node[above left] at (3.15,1.25) {$E$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\triangle ABC$ is isosceles with $AB = AC$ and $M$ is the midpoint of $BC$. Which congruence test proves $\triangle ABM \cong \triangle ACM$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc}
\tikzset{tk/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}},tk2/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (-2pt,-4pt)--(-2pt,4pt);\draw (2pt,-4pt)--(2pt,4pt);}}}}}
