\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (M) at (2.2,0);
\draw[tk2] (A)--(B);
\draw[tk2] (A)--(C);
\draw[tk] (B)--(M);
\draw[tk] (M)--(C);
\draw (A)--(M);

\node[above] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In rhombus $ABCD$ the diagonals meet at $E$, and $\triangle ABE \cong \triangle ADE$ has been proved. Which statement correctly completes the proof that the diagonals are perpendicular?
